Signed-off-by: Steven Rostedt (Google) <rostedt@goodmis.org>

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the inability of event probes (eprobes) to handle the "comm" and "COMM" symbols properly, leading to a NULL pointer dereference when these symbols were referenced in an event that did not have a corresponding field. This inconsistency with kprobes and uprobes resulted in crashes when attempting to access data that was not available in the event context.

